pi-web-access — vendored bundled extension
==========================================

Upstream package : pi-web-access 0.35.0 (MIT)
Upstream author  : Nico Bailon (https://github.com/nicobailon/pi-web-access)
License          : MIT — see LICENSE (copied verbatim from upstream)

This directory is OMA's bundled copy of the pi-web-access extension:

  upstream/        exact npm tarball content of pi-web-access@0.35.0,
                   unmodified — the integrity-pinned source snapshot. Every
                   tarball .ts file, LICENSE, README.md, CHANGELOG.md and
                   SECURITY.md matches the source commit named in
                   manifest.json byte-for-byte; package.json differs only
                   in upstream's own postpublish entry rewrite
                   ("./index.ts" -> "./dist"), and dist/ is the bundled
                   build upstream publishes (vendored for provenance,
                   never loaded).
  upstream-tests/  the upstream test tree from the source commit named in
                   manifest.json (the npm tarball ships no tests); vendored
                   so OMA's ported boundary tests can cite and re-derive
                   upstream's fixtures. Not wired into npm test wholesale —
                   upstream's suite needs the upstream repo layout and hits
                   the network for most provider tests.
  node_modules/    the pinned runtime dependency closure — the resolved
                   production install of upstream's declared dependencies
                   (@modelcontextprotocol/sdk, @mozilla/readability,
                   defuddle, linkedom, p-limit, promise.try, turndown,
                   undici, unpdf and their transitive deps), byte-exact to
                   the npm-installed tree at vendoring time and named with
                   lockfile integrity in manifest.json — kept separate from
                   anything a user-installed Pi package would resolve.
                   Peer/host API packages (@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent,
                   @earendil-works/pi-tui, @earendil-works/pi-ai, typebox)
                   are NOT vendored: they resolve to OMA's own install.
  runtime/         compiled JavaScript + declarations of upstream's .ts
                   modules, generated by scripts/vendor-pi-web-access.mjs:
                   relative ".ts" specifiers are rewritten to ".js" before
                   tsc emit (Node's loader needs them), then OMA's declared
                   divergence splices are applied — the web policy seams
                   (credential commands, browser cookies, gh CLI, local
                   file fetch, curator workflows), the egress proxy pin
                   (including the vendored-undici dispatcher surface the
                   adapter installs through utils.js's re-export) and
                   the init-config overlay that pins the Society surface
                   (eager registration, fixed tool names, no commands, no
                   answer mode, no workflows). Generated, hash-pinned input
                   — not authored OMA code. Every upstream module is
                   emitted; OMA's adapter (src/extension/web-tools.ts)
                   verifies the bundle, installs the policy, then drives
                   upstream's own extension factory through a facade that
                   admits only the four web_research tool registrations.
  manifest.json    generated bundle manifest: per-file SHA-256, byte
                   counts and a deterministic whole-bundle digest, plus
                   the upstream name/version/commit, npm tarball
                   integrity/shasum metadata and the pinned dependency
                   closure.

No part of this bundle is fetched, installed or cloned at run time.
